From 472c24c56ef9ab91db09ace159ee4da8c544c7b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Nijmeh <tylernij@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Aug 2019 21:40:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 45/57] mm/compaction: Increase fragmentation index

Imply that memory fragmentation is more often responsible for failed
memory allocations rather than insufficient memory capacity. For the
end user, background tasks will be killed less often (if possible) and a
compaction will be preferred over triggering an OOM event.

Fragmentation interacts poorly with the VIDC and MSM Camera subsystem,
both of which make heavy use of contiguous memory blocks.

The case goes as follows:
- User is already low on available memory (70%+)
- User attempts to render multiple videos in quick succession
- Memory allocation fails due to lack of contiguous memory for the video
- OOM is triggered over compaction
- Important userspace task killed

Biasing the fragmentation threshold makes more contiguous memory blocks
available for contig-intensive processes; more userspace tasks remain
running under VIDC and MSM Camera loads.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Nijmeh <tylernij@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Rapherion Rollerscaperers <rapherion@raphielgang.org>
Signed-off-by: techyminati <sinha.aryan03@gmail.com>
